body:
I took a first look at this an want to narrow the extent of when this happens down to the specific case mentioned in the above reproduction (geopoint array inside an object array).
It's important that the parent of the geopoint field is also an array. Note e.g. that this works as expected (tested on 7.17):

```
PUT test/_doc/1
{
  "results": {
      "value": [
        {
          "lat": 0,
          "lon": 0
        },
        {
            "lat" : 1,
            "lon" : 1            
        }
      ],
      "foo" : [1,2]

    }  
}


POST /test*/_search
{
  "_source": false,
  "fields": [
    "*"
  ]
}

--->

"fields": {
                    "results.value": [
                        {
                            "coordinates": [
                                0,
                                0
                            ],
                            "type": "Point"
                        },
                        {
                            "coordinates": [
                                1,
                                1
                            ],
                            "type": "Point"
                        }
                    ],
                    "results.foo": [
                        1,
                        2
                    ]
                }
```
Also, other field types (e.g. numeric types) work nested in an outer array as in:
```
PUT test/_doc/1
{
  "results": [{
       "foo" : [1,2]
    } ]
}
```
